        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the lack of proper deallocation of the `cpumask_var_t` variables (`available_cpus` and `non_intr_cpus`) after their allocation in the `_dev_comp_vect_mappings_create` function. This oversight led to a memory leak, as the allocated memory was not being freed, resulting in unreferenced objects accumulating over time.

        Commit message:
        RDMA/hfi1: Fix memory leak in _dev_comp_vect_mappings_create

Make sure to free the allocated cpumask_var_t's to avoid the following
reported memory leak by kmemleak:

$ cat /sys/kernel/debug/kmemleak
